foreign  welcome to Harry Potter Theory Lord  Voldemort and gallet Grindelwald are the  two most powerful dark wizards of modern  history and their lives were eerily  similar both of them shared a common foe  a Helper stumbledore and both of them  shamelessly butchered their fellow  Wizards and witches in pursuit of power  but when you look at the pair of dark  Wizards you might be surprised to find  out that there's quite a bit that  separates them from their individual  manifestos to their actual magical  powers Voldemort and Grindelwald  couldn't have been more different today  we're going to shed some light on those  differences and find out what divided  these two wizards 9. Voldemort's Elona  to put it simply Lord Voldemort is a  loner noun that obviously doesn't mean  he was technically alone all the time  from the first day attended Hogwarts  School of Witchcraft and Wizardry Tom  Riddle demonstrated his remarkable  Charisma and cultivated a cult that  followed him around from class to class  but those students many of whom would  evolve into murderous Death Eaters were  simply followers Voldemort ever  considered them his peers and certainly  not his friends and it makes sense if  you think about it Lord voldel was  conceived while his father was Bewitched  by a love potion according to law The  Offspring of such unions were incapable  of love and if they ever reached  adulthood could be considered sociopaths  by contrast much of galic grindelwald's  early life was defined by love and  passion his partnership with Albus  Dumbledore is what drove Grindelwald to  pursue the Hallows and pushed for the  end of the magical laws that restricted  Wizards and witches even after all of  his fights when Grindelwald was over 100  years in age he likely looked back at  his life with regrets and probably  wished he could have done it all  differently 8. Threat Level after seeing  the vicious battles at Harry Potter and  his friends endured it's hard to imagine  that Voldemort was anything less than a  global threat  but if you actually look at the details  of the Death Eaters and their campaigns  the group limited their activities to  Great Britain for the most part  Voldemort was interested in overthrowing  the ministry of magic and revamping The  Wizarding World in the UK he probably  had greater interests and wanted to  waltz into France and Continental Europe  after securing England but during the  events of the Harry Potter books  Voldemort was firmly fixed in the  British Isles and when we compare this  to Grindelwald we'll see that Tom  Riddle's Campaign Of Terror seems far  smaller by comparison Grindelwald  Revolution stretched across the globe  from the shores of the United States to  the streets of the French Capital  Gellert wanted to overthrow the  international Wizarding order and so he  staged a multi-front campaign to do so  7. their reign during the second  Wizarding War Lord Voldemort managed to  claim power for just about a year during  that time Harry Potter Ron Weasley and  Hermione Granger tried to finish what  Albus Dumbledore had started hunting and  destroying all the remaining horcruxes  at times it seemed like the three  Hogwarts students would never find the  evil relics that held blood Voldemort's  soul but in the end they succeeded after  only a few months Voldemort was not only  overthrown but he was killed Voldemort's  single year of rule paled in comparison  to Grindelwald although Voldemort  controlled the ministry during his Reign  might have been stronger Grindelwald and  his acolytes were active for over two  decades during that time the dark wizard  LED political and Guerrilla campaigns  against his fellow Wizards unlike the  Death Eaters who only represented a  small affluent group of pure blood  families within Britain grindelwald's  followers were far more vast gallet was  almost like a political party of his own  with thousands of supporters around the  globe 6. who was more evil to be honest  most Wizards would admit that Lord  Voldemort was just about the most evil  sorcerer in existence when Hagrid  Dumbledore or any number of Harry's  mentors talked about Voldemort they  often claimed that he was more than just  simply evil as if there were no words  that could describe the depravity that  Tom Riddle had reached even though galic  Grindelwald was No Angel by any stretch  of the imagination the crimes he  committed were reasonable by comparison  grindelwald's goals after all were once  shared by Albus Dumbledore and they were  far more political than Voldemort's own  selfish desires Grindelwald wanted to  free The Wizarding World from the rules  that kept them hidden he believed that  the Wizarding World should be the most  powerful Society on the planet and that  Muggles and their own governments should  exist beneath them while on the surface  that sounds like something Voldemort  would agree with Tom Riddle's methods  were far more Craven he never showed  compassion and would never have  displayed regret as Grindelwald seemed  to do at the end of his life 5. horcrux  versus Hallows one of the biggest  differences between these two dark  Wizards was the way they sought power  both were obsessed with increasing their  magical abilities and both set out on  quest to gather the Deathly Hallows but  Grindelwald limited himself to those  magical relics and eventually became the  second most powerful owner of the Elder  Wand that hallow which Voldemort  desperately tried to claim for himself  would be the Dark Lord's undoing when he  tried to use it to kill Harry Potter but  unlike Voldemort Grindelwald didn't dare  undergo the complex procedure to split  his soul and create horcruxes and if you  think about why there's really only a  handful of answers some historians might  suggest that Grindelwald simply didn't  possess the knowledge to create these  dark enchantments but considering that  galactron the world's magical abilities  and expertise was only narrowly  surpassed by Albert Dumbledore this  historical take seems pretty unlikely in  this case the more obvious case appears  to be true Grindelwald didn't create  horcruxes because he didn't want to  perhaps he simply wasn't evil enough to  even consider the selfish murder of  another person in order to split his  soul or maybe he thought he'd be more  powerful without horcruxes although  there could be another reason 4.  attitude towards death compared to  Voldemort Grindelwald showed almost no  fear of death this might be another  reason why the famed dark Wizard never  created horcruxes of his own when Tom  Riddle stared into a bogart the magical  creature that showed you your own  greatest fear the dark wizard was  shocked to find his own corpse he didn't  see a massive spider like Ron Weasley or  the death of a loved one like Apple's  Dumbledore no Voldemort saw his own  demise in the Bogut Lord Voldemort split  his soul seven times and sought to  master the dark arts because he feared  his own death and Grindelwald didn't by  the end of his life when Lord snotkin  news jail cell Grindelwald laughed in  the younger Dark Lord's face and  encouraged riddle to kill him although  Grindelwald was well over 100 years in  age by that time so he might have  welcomed the idea of passing still it's  hard to imagine Lord Voldemort ever  achieving such a state of Zen when it  comes to his own mortality 3. schooling  it might shock you to know that garlic  Grindelwald and the famed co-founder of  Hogwarts salazaren bear no relation at  all throughout the medieval and modern  eras many of the most terrifying dark  Wizards passed through the Slytherin  house at Hogwarts School of Witchcraft  and Wizardry in fact it's almost hard to  imagine a dark Wizard or witch could  exist without first having been sorted  into Southern first but not only was  Grindelwald never enrolled in Hogwarts  he attended a completely different  School The durmstrang Institute a place  he was later expelled from for  performing twisted and dark experiments  on fellow students  2. parcel tongue speaking to serpents is  almost a prerequisite when it comes to  being a dark wizard but unlike herpa the  fowl and Lord Voldemort gelat  Grindelwald never showed an ability for  parcel tongue that skill which was such  an heirloom for The Heirs of Southern  was only one of a few that Grindelwald  never managed to master although  considering how much the dark wizard  achieved his inability to converse with  snakes wasn't that big of a deal 1.  dueling do you think galic Grindelwald  was a better duelist than Lord Voldemort  that might seem like a foolish question  to ask especially when you recall the  exact circumstances of grindelwald's  death he was executed by Lord Voldemort  after all but that wasn't really a fair  Showdown gallet was at least 115 years  old at the time and he was completely  unarmed although Wizards and witches  lived unusually long lives Grindelwald  was still several decades past his prime  when we compared Lord Voldemort's own  dueling achievements against those of a  prime gallet it's surprising to see just  how much Grindelwald shines by  comparison both of these dark Wizards  shared Albus Dumbledore as an adversary  but Voldemort never seemed to get the  better of the Hogwarts Headmaster  Grindelwald on the other hand nearly  defeated him during their famous Jewel  at the end of the second world war of  course there were reasons for  Voldemort's losses as well as  grindelwald's near win still most  magical historians would favor  Grindelwald in this comparison if you  want a greater breakdown of who is the  more powerful wizard go and check out my  video Voldemort vs Grindelwald who is  more powerful Link in the description  and there you have it nine ways in which  Lord Voldemort in garlic Grindelwald are  different what do you think how do you  think they're different let me know in  the comments below until next time  remember when we allow ourselves to be  consumed by anger the only victim is  ourself  [Music]

